music BGM26B.mp3
text We once again walk the earth, searching for scrap.
text ..."You shouldn't wander off that far away from me."
text She stops me when I try to walk ahead.
text Why not? I wonder as I turn back.
text ..."Because you won't be able to return."
text I turn around once again and look far into the distance...
text At the plains that stretch out forever.
setvar strS[1000] = "KURO"
setvar intA[1000] = 1
if intA[1000] == 0
	goto s34
fi
goto 35
label s34
setvar strS[1000] = ""
label 35
setvar strS[1001] = "NONE"
setvar intF[1113] = intF[1112]
bgload {$strS[1000]}.jpg 98
if intF[1113] == 1
	if strS[1000] < "C"
		setimg {$strS[1004]}.png -7 -7
	fi
fi
text But once I get used to junk-hunting, I start becoming engrossed in it.
text By the time I've climbed the hill, I realize that I'm alone.
text I begin to panic and climb back up the other side, but she's nowhere to be found.
text I can't see behind me well because of all of the ups and downs in the terrain.
text Unable to even scream, I begin to amble around on my own.
text I don't know what direction home is in any longer.
text Am I getting farther away from it, or am I getting closer?
text I stumble, then trip over the hill.
text I fall face-up onto the earth.
setvar strS[1000] = "BG307"
setvar intA[1000] = 1
if intA[1000] == 0
	goto s35
fi
goto 36
label s35
setvar strS[1000] = ""
label 36
setvar strS[1001] = "NONE"
setvar intF[1113] = intF[1112]
bgload {$strS[1000]}.jpg 98
if intF[1113] == 1
	if strS[1000] < "C"
		setimg {$strS[1004]}.png -7 -7
	fi
fi
text The clouds are spread out in the sky before me.
text They've taken odd, ominous shapes.
text I'm not familiar with these ones.
text I'm certain the clouds in the place where I was with her weren't like this.
text This place is such a different one...
text Fear begins to grip me.
text ──"Because you won't be able to return."
text I remember her words.
text There are still many things I don't know about this world.
text Perhaps the land doesn't go on forever like I think?
text Perhaps it becomes twisted at some point.
text Even if I walk toward one of the forests off in the distance, I may end up arriving in a completely different one.
text Junk is scattered all around me.
text If she were by my side, I'm sure I'd happily grab it out of the ground.
text But now, it's nothing more than one part of a terrifying world.
text I stand. It's all I can do.
text Where is this place...?
text Does she still exist in the same time as me?
text I've even started questioning that.
text I should go back.
text I look up at the hill I've tumbled down.
text I see a small shadow with a light to its back.
text It's looking down at me from the very top.
text An animal.
text So they've even come here.
text Its body is small, almost as if it's a newborn.
text Just then, something strikes me as strange.
text Is that animal looking at me?
text Those things don't act on their own volition.
text They're nothing more than beings who coldly eat up the greenery around them.
text But one is staring right down at me.
text Almost as if it has a will of its own.
text I slowly climb the hill.
text The tiny shadow doesn't run.
text When I stand next to it, the animal no larger than my foot turns aside and scurries off.
text Was it waiting for me?
text I pause for a second, then decide to chase after it as if I've just remembered something.
setvar strS[1000] = "KURO"
setvar intA[1000] = 1
